{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.QJucysMurphy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QJucysMurphy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeAlgebra","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HoefsmitRep","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":47,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.barSymJMSum_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.barSymJMSum_central","kind":"theorem","line":1075,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L1075-L1086","doc":"**`barSymJMSum` is central**, given `q · qi = 1` — sorry-free.\n\nThe hypothesis is not decoration.  `σ_i` commutes with the pair `L_i + L_{i+1}` only up to the\nresidue `(1 − q·qi)(σ_i L_i − L_i σ_i)` (see `pair_comm`), and without `q · qi = 1` the element\n`qJMInv` is not an inverse of `qJM` at all.  A hypothesis-free version of this statement was\ncarried here as a `sorry` until 2026-08-17 (bean `qou-gjg6`); it is not provable by this route,\nand it was deleted rather than left standing as proof debt it never was. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.cellContentCoshSum_eq_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.cellContentCoshSum_eq_bracket","kind":"theorem","line":1022,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L1022-L1044","doc":"**`cellContentCoshSum` in bracket form** (sorry-free): with `q ≠ 0`,\n  `Σ_{c∈λ}(q^{2c}+q^{−2c}) = Σ_{c∈λ}(q^{c}−q^{−c})² + 2·|λ|`.\nAfter factoring `[c]_q = (q^{c}−q^{−c})/(q−q⁻¹)` this is `(q−q⁻¹)²·Σ_c[c]_q² + 2n`: the two bar-even\nbrackets coincide up to the bar-even scalar `(q−q⁻¹)²` and the λ-independent shift `2n = 2|λ|`, so\n**neither is a spectral degree of freedom** (bean `qou-ck0g` / `qou-8vt2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.cellContentCoshSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.cellContentCoshSum","kind":"def","line":1016,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L1016-L1020","doc":"**The cosh sum over the cells of `λ`** — the block eigenvalue candidate for `barSymJMSum` on the\nirreducible `ρ_λ`: `Σ_{c∈λ}(q^{2c} + q^{−2c})`, `c = cellContent` the content of each cell (a\n`ℤ`-power, so the base ring is a `Field` — §7c: this is the archimedean/observation side, `q ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.barSym_block_sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.barSym_block_sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1003,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L1003-L1012","doc":"**Block-level cosh–bracket identity** (sorry-free).  For `a, b : ι → R` with `a i · b i = 1`\non `s`: `Σ_{i∈s}(a i² + b i²) = Σ_{i∈s}(a i − b i)² + 2·|s|`.  The `Finset` sum of\n`cosh_eq_sq_bracket_add_two`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_seminormalRep21_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_seminormalRep21_one","kind":"theorem","line":980,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L980-L992","doc":"**`(2,1)` eigenvalue** (sorry-free, over `ℝ`): `ρ_{(2,1)}(L_1) = diag(q², q⁻²)`.\n`L_1 = σ_0²` and `ρ_{(2,1)}(σ_0) = S0 = diag(q, −q⁻¹)`, so `ρ_{(2,1)}(L_1) = S0² = diag(q², q⁻²)`.\nThe diagonal entries are `q^{2·(+1)}` and `q^{2·(−1)}`: the two SYT of `(2,1)` whose cell holding\nentry `2` has content `+1` (row-sharing) resp. `−1` (column-sharing).  This is the first\n*genuinely 2-dimensional* witness of the `q^{2c}` convention.  Ref: [ram1997] Thm 4.1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.barSymJMSum_rhoTriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.barSymJMSum_rhoTriv","kind":"theorem","line":967,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L967-L976","doc":"**Block eigenvalue of `Θ` on the trivial rep** (sorry-free): `ρ_triv(Θ_n) = Σ_{k=0}^{n}(q^{2k}+qi^{2k})`.\nThis is the \"cosh\" block eigenvalue `Σ_{c∈λ}(q^{2c}+q^{−2c})` realised concretely for the one-row\nshape `(N)` (contents `c = 0, …, n`) — the bar-even scalar that bean `qou-8vt2` consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_rhoSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_rhoSign","kind":"theorem","line":956,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L956-L965","doc":"**Sign-rep eigenvalue** (sorry-free): `ρ_sign(L_k) = qi^{2k}` for `k ≤ n`.\nOn the one-column shape `(1^N)` the cell holding entry `k+1` has content `−k`, so once `q·qi = 1`\nthis reads `q^{2·(−k)} = q^{−2k}` — the `q^{2c}` convention on the antisymmetric channel.\nRef: [ram1997] Thm 4.1; [murphy1992]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_rhoTriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_rhoTriv","kind":"theorem","line":947,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L947-L954","doc":"**Trivial-rep eigenvalue of the inverse Murphy element** (sorry-free): `ρ_triv(L_k⁻¹) = qi^{2k}`\nfor `k ≤ n`.  With `q·qi = 1` this is `q^{−2k}`, the bar-partner of `qJM_rhoTriv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_rhoTriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_rhoTriv","kind":"theorem","line":936,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L936-L945","doc":"**Trivial-rep eigenvalue** (sorry-free): `ρ_triv(L_k) = q^{2k}` for `k ≤ n`.\nThe Murphy element `L_k` acts on the (unique) SYT of the one-row shape `(N)` by `q^{2c}` with\n`c = k` the content of the cell holding entry `k+1`.  Realises the `q^{2c}` convention on the\nsymmetric channel.  Ref: [ram1997] Thm 4.1; [murphy1992]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.rhoSign_σInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.rhoSign_σInv","kind":"theorem","line":930,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L930-L934","doc":"`ρ_sign(σ_i⁻¹) = −q` (sorry-free): `σ_i⁻¹ ↦ (−qi) − (q − qi) = −q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.rhoTriv_σInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.rhoTriv_σInv","kind":"theorem","line":924,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L924-L928","doc":"`ρ_triv(σ_i⁻¹) = qi` (sorry-free): `σ_i⁻¹ = σ_i − (q − qi)·1 ↦ q − (q − qi) = qi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.barSymJMSum_zero_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.barSymJMSum_zero_eq","kind":"theorem","line":872,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L872-L876","doc":"`Θ_0 = L_0 + L_0⁻¹ = 1 + 1 = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.barSymJMSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.barSymJMSum","kind":"def","line":863,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L863-L870","doc":"**The bar-symmetrised Jucys–Murphy sum** `Θ_n := Σ_{k=0}^{n} (L_k + L_k⁻¹)`.\n\nThis is the principled bar-even generator for the q-heat kernel: the bar\ninvolution `q ↦ q⁻¹` sends `L_k ↦ L_k⁻¹`, so each summand `L_k + L_k⁻¹`\nis bar-invariant, and hence `Θ_n` is bar-even.  Its block eigenvalue on the\nirreducible `ρ_λ` is `Σ_{c ∈ λ} (q^{2c} + q^{−2c})`, the cosh form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_commute","kind":"theorem","line":833,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L833-L850","doc":"**[GAP] The Murphy elements commute pairwise** — they generate the commutative\nGelfand–Tsetlin subalgebra `GZ_{n+1} ⊂ H_{n+1}(q)`.\n\n-- Ref: [murphy1992] — the q-deformed Murphy operators generate a maximal commutative\n-- subalgebra of `H_{n+1}(q)`.  Also [ram1997] Corollary 2.4.\n-- The classical proof (the `L_k` are simultaneously diagonalised by the\n-- seminormal basis) lifts verbatim to the q-deformed setting.\n-- Blocked on: the general seminormal rep (bean SW-4 residual). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_sum_comm_sigma'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_sum_comm_sigma'","kind":"theorem","line":821,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L821-L829","doc":"**`Σ_{k≤n} L_k` is central**, with no side hypothesis on `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_sum_comm_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_sum_comm_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":809,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L809-L819","doc":"**`Σ_{k≤n} L_k⁻¹` is central.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_comm_of_rows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_comm_of_rows","kind":"theorem","line":777,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L777-L807","doc":"Generic Finset assembly: a family `F` whose `{i,i+1}` pair commutes with\n`σ_i` and whose other members commute individually has a central sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_pair_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_pair_comm","kind":"theorem","line":768,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L768-L775","doc":"Row 2 for the inverse family: `σ_i` commutes with `L_i⁻¹ + L_{i+1}⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_comm_sigma_high","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_comm_sigma_high","kind":"theorem","line":761,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L761-L766","doc":"Row 3 for the inverse family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_comm_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_comm_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":754,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L754-L759","doc":"Row 1 for the inverse family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.comm_inv_of_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.comm_inv_of_comm","kind":"theorem","line":744,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L744-L752","doc":"Commuting with a two-sided unit transfers to its inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.comm_σInv_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.comm_σInv_iff","kind":"theorem","line":737,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L737-L742","doc":"**Commuting with `σ_i` and with `σ_i⁻¹` are the same condition** — `σInv` is\n`σ - (q-qi)•1`, a polynomial in `σ`, so the two differ by a central term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.σInv_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.σInv_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":725,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L725-L735","doc":"`σ_i⁻¹` satisfies the same quadratic with `d ↦ -d`: `σ⁻¹² = (qi-q)·σ⁻¹ + 1`\nwhen `q·qi = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_sum_comm_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_sum_comm_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":692,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L692-L723","doc":"**The first Murphy power sum `Σ_{k≤n} L_k` is central.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_comm_sigma_high","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_comm_sigma_high","kind":"theorem","line":616,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L616-L675","doc":"**`σ_i` commutes with `L_k` for every `k ≥ i + 2`.** The third and last row\nneeded for centrality. Not far commutation: at `k = i+2` the outer generator\n`σ_{i+1}` is adjacent to `σ_i`, and the base case runs on the braid relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_pair_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_pair_comm","kind":"theorem","line":604,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L604-L614","doc":"**`σ_i` commutes with `L_i + L_{i+1}`** when `q · qi = 1`. Neither summand\nis `σ_i`-invariant; the pair is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.pair_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.pair_comm","kind":"theorem","line":592,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L592-L602","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_commute_proved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_commute_proved","kind":"theorem","line":542,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L542-L554","doc":"**The Murphy elements commute pairwise — unconditionally.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":511,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L511-L540","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.adjacent_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.adjacent_step","kind":"theorem","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L468-L501","doc":"**The adjacent case at `k` follows from the adjacent case at `k-1`.**\nNo invertibility, no quadratic relation — braid, `s`-commutation, and the\nprevious adjacent instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_one_two_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_one_two_commute","kind":"theorem","line":442,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L442-L466","doc":"**`L_1` and `L_2` commute — unconditionally, from the braid relation alone.**\nThe `k = 1` instance of the adjacent case, where `B = L_0 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.braid_pow_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.braid_pow_three","kind":"theorem","line":434,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L434-L440","doc":"The residual commutation at `B = 1`, i.e. `(ts)³ = (st)³`. Braid alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.adjacent_reduce","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.adjacent_reduce","kind":"theorem","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L413-L432","doc":"**The adjacent case, reduced.** Both sides of `L_k L_{k+1} = L_{k+1} L_k`\ncollapse — using *only* the braid relation and `σ_k`-commutation — to one word\nconjugated by `s`. Here `t = σ_{k-1}`, `s = σ_k`, `B = L_{k-1}`, `A = t B t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_commute_of_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_commute_of_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":342,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L342-L388","doc":"**Full commutativity follows from the adjacent case alone.**\n\nEverything except `L_k L_{k+1} = L_{k+1} L_k` is bookkeeping: `σ_{j-1}` commutes\nwith `L_i` as soon as `i + 1 ≤ j - 1` (`qJM_comm_sigma`), which peels one step\noff `L_j = σ_{j-1} L_{j-1} σ_{j-1}` and hands the rest to the induction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_comm_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_comm_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L309-L340","doc":"`σ_m` commutes with `L_k` whenever `k + 1 ≤ m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.sq_bracket_eq_cosh_sub_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.sq_bracket_eq_cosh_sub_two","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L252-L259","doc":"**Symmetry form** of the cosh–bracket identity: `(a − b)² = a² + b² − 2`.\n\nUseful when the LHS (the bracket form) is the primary, and the RHS (cosh minus\nconstant) is the target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.cosh_eq_sq_bracket_add_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.cosh_eq_sq_bracket_add_two","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L239-L250","doc":"**Cleared-denominators cosh–bracket identity** (sorry-free).\n\nFor any `a, b ∈ R` with `a · b = 1`:\n  `a² + b² = (a − b)² + 2`.\n\nInstantiate with `a := q^c`, `b := q^{−c}` to obtain the per-cell identity\n  `q^{2c} + q^{−2c} = (q^c − q^{−c})² + 2 = (q − q⁻¹)² · [c]_q² + 2`,\nthe last step by `[c]_q = (q^c − q^{−c})/(q − q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_mul_qJM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_mul_qJM","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L196-L218","doc":"**`qJMInv` is the left inverse of `qJM`** when `q · qi = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_mul_qJMInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_mul_qJMInv","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L160-L194","doc":"**`qJMInv` is the right inverse of `qJM`** when `q · qi = 1`.\n\nProof: straightforward induction on `k`. Base: `1 · 1 = 1`. Step: by\nassociativity `σ L σ · σ⁻¹ L⁻¹ σ⁻¹ = σ · (L L⁻¹) · σ⁻¹ → σ · σ⁻¹ → 1`,\nusing the inductive hypothesis `L_k · L_k⁻¹ = 1` and `σ_mul_σInv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_succ","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L155-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv_zero","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L152-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJMInv","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L143-L150","doc":"**Inverse Murphy elements** `L_k⁻¹ ∈ H_{n+1}(q)`, defined recursively:\n`L_0⁻¹ = 1`,   `L_{k+1}⁻¹ = σInv_k · L_k⁻¹ · σInv_k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_one_expand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_one_expand","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L124-L129","doc":"`L_1` expanded via the quadratic relation: `σ_0² = (q − qi)·σ_0 + q·qi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_one","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L118-L122","doc":"`L_1 = σ_0²` (when the algebra has at least one generator). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_succ","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L112-L116","doc":"Recursion step: `L_{k+1} = σ_k · L_k · σ_k` for `k < n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM_zero","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L108-L110","doc":"`L_0 = 1` (the identity element of `H_{n+1}(q)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.qJM","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QJucysMurphy.lean#L91-L106","doc":"**The Murphy elements** `L_k ∈ H_{n+1}(q)` (`= Hecke K q qi n`), defined recursively:\n  `L_0 = 1`,   `L_{k+1} = σ_k · L_k · σ_k`.\n\n`Hecke K q qi n` has `n` generators `σ_0, …, σ_{n−1}`, corresponding to the Hecke algebra\n`H_{n+1}(q)` (the symmetric group `S_{n+1}` has `n` adjacent transpositions).  There are\n`n + 1` Murphy elements `L_0, …, L_n`.  For indices beyond `n`, the recursion freezes\n(no generator `σ_k` exists); those elements are semantically meaningless.\n\nThe recursion `L_{k+1} = σ_k L_k σ_k` is the q-analogue of the classical Jucys–Murphy\nrecursion in `MonoidAlgebra k (Equiv.Perm (Fin n))` (see `QOU.BraidKnot.jucysMurphy`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}